.Fn mbt_storage_memory_length "struct mbt_storage_memory *m"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt struct mbt_storage
is a reference-counted object that holds torrent data.
Sessions and torrents take their own references, so the caller can drop its
reference after it passes the storage to a session or torrent.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_storage_new
makes a storage with one reference from a
.Vt struct mbt_storage_ops
and a context pointer.
It returns
.Dv NULL
if it cannot allocate memory.
.Fn mbt_storage_ref
adds a reference.
.Fn mbt_storage_unref
removes one, and calls the
.Fa destroy
operation when the last reference goes.
Both accept
.Dv NULL .
.Sh BACKEND OPERATIONS
.Fa open
receives the context and a torrent, and sets its last argument to a
.Vt struct mbt_storage_handle
that is not
.Dv NULL .
The torrent passes this handle to
.Fa write_piece ,
.Fa read_piece ,
.Fa have_piece
and
.Fa close .
The torrent calls
.Fa close
before it drops its reference to the storage.
.Fa destroy
is optional.
.Pp
.Fa remove
and
.Fa exists
are optional.
.Fa remove
deletes the data of an open torrent.
The handle stays valid for
.Fa close .
.Fa exists
returns 1 if data for the torrent is already present, and 0 if not.
.Xr mbt_torrent_move_storage 3
needs
.Fa remove
on both storages, and uses
.Fa exists
on the target.
.Sh FILE STORAGE
.Fn mbt_storage_file_new
makes a storage for files under
.Fa data_dir .
It holds any number of torrents.
A single-file torrent uses
.Pa data_dir/name .
A multi-file torrent uses
.Pa data_dir/torrent_name/path .
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EEXIST
if a file path is in use by a torrent that is open on this storage.
.Sh MEMORY STORAGE
The memory backend holds one torrent at a time in a flat buffer.
A second
.Fa open
fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_new
makes a memory storage.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_destroy
drops the reference that
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_new
made.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_storage
returns the storage and adds no reference.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_put_file
writes into the buffer at an offset, and grows the buffer if necessary.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_get_file
reads from the buffer at an offset.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_data
returns the buffer.
.Fn mbt_storage_memory_length
returns the size of the buffer.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3 ,
